 # HANDOFF
 
+## Latest update: mechanical iteration_limit_reached enforcement
+
+This pass adds `scripts/execution-harness.js`, a minimal, dependency-free Node script
+(only `fs`/`path`) that mechanically enforces exactly one Execution Mode run boundary:
+`iteration_limit_reached`. It reads `execution.current_iteration` and
+`execution.max_iterations` from `.l00prite/heartbeat.json`; its `advance` subcommand
+increments and persists the counter, or refuses (non-zero exit, a message naming the
+`iteration_limit_reached` boundary, and no write at all) once
+`current_iteration >= max_iterations`. The refusal runs in the script's own control
+flow — an unconditional `if` before any write — not something an LLM is merely asked to
+respect. `scripts/execution-harness.test.js` is a self-contained smoke test (built-in
+`assert`/`child_process`/`fs`/`os`/`path` only) that empirically proves the boundary
+refusal, the byte-identical file state after a refusal, and the self-modification guard
+across a sequence of calls.
+
+### Why scope is fixed to one boundary
+
+l00prite's roadmap has long described "a runtime harness that mechanically enforces run
+boundaries and iteration budgets" as future work (see the prior `HANDOFF.md`/`README.md`/
+`CLAUDE.md`/`.l00prite/todos.md` entries below). This pass narrows that from an aspiration
+to a real, working script — but only for `iteration_limit_reached`. That boundary is a
+pure numeric comparison (`current_iteration >= max_iterations`) with no judgment call
+involved, so it is the one boundary a small script can enforce correctly and completely.
+The other eight (`definition_of_done_met`, `human_review_gate`,
+`destructive_operation_required`, `ambiguous_requirements`, `unfixable_failing_tests`,
+`missing_secrets_or_credentials`, `lock_lease_conflict`, `stop_signal`) require judgment —
+"is the Definition of Done genuinely verified?", "is this operation destructive?" — that
+this script does not attempt. They remain protocol-only, validator-checked prompt text in
+`templates/l00prite/prompts/execute-loop.md` and its mirrors.
+
+### What was deliberately left alone, and why
+
+- `scripts/validate-l00prite.js` and `.claude/commands/build-loop.md` — both are
+  human-review-gated per `CLAUDE.md` section 6; nothing in this task's Definition of Done
+  required opening either gate (the validator only needed to keep passing, not gain new
+  checks), so neither was touched.
+- `templates/l00prite/prompts/execute-loop.md` and its six byte-identical mirrors — the
+  iteration protocol still says "increment `execution.current_iteration`" as agent
+  instruction text; it does not yet call `scripts/execution-harness.js advance`. Wiring it
+  in is a separate, larger change (a 7-location byte-identical prose edit plus
+  revalidation) tracked as a follow-up in `.l00prite/todos.md`, not done here to keep this
+  pass minimal and to avoid two double-counting/scope hazards recorded there: the manual
+  increment instruction must be *replaced*, not kept alongside, when the wiring happens;
+  and the harness is deliberately agnostic to `execution.enabled`/`should_continue`, so it
+  must never become the run's sole gate without a conscious decision that `stop_signal`
+  stays unenforced.
+- `templates/` scaffolding — the harness is a repo-local dev tool for l00prite's own repo,
+  the same way `scripts/validate-l00prite.js` is not copied into scaffolded projects.
+  Whether target projects should eventually get a harness like this too is a bigger product
+  question, left to `.l00prite/todos.md`.
+
+### Honest limitation
+
+This is mechanical enforcement only for callers that route iteration advancement through
+`scripts/execution-harness.js` and treat a non-zero exit as a hard stop. It cannot stop a
+caller that bypasses the script entirely — hand-editing `heartbeat.json` directly, or
+editing the script itself. No userland script in a filesystem-writable agent environment
+can prevent that; this is the same cooperative-not-enforced philosophy `LOCKING.md` already
+discloses for `lock.json`.
+
+### Updated remaining gaps (supersedes the blanket claim in the v1.1 section below)
+
+- Execution Mode's invariants are validator-enforced prompt text for eight of the nine run
+  boundaries; a non-compliant model can still ignore those eight. `iteration_limit_reached`
+  is the exception — mechanically enforced by `scripts/execution-harness.js`, not yet wired
+  into `execute-loop.md`'s live iteration protocol.
+- The lock/lease convention is still cooperative, not filesystem-enforced.
+- No automated CI runs the validator (or the new test) on this repo yet.
+- No event ingestion: events are still hand-authored JSON.
+
